# HY300 (2023 firmware) -- the MagCubic HY300 in the classic case with a 2023 ADT-3 firmware: a 720p panel (0x34), the
# HY350 family's DRAM block at 792 MHz, two units with two boot packages (variants/). fw202306 is the issue #8 unit
# (GitHub `erfrizzera`, 02.-06.11.2026: U-Boot and ARISC of 2023-06-25, a display.bin revision of its own); fw202312 the
# issue #11 unit (GitHub `Souks`, 11.11.2026: U-Boot of 2023-12-08, ARISC of 2023-12-27, the "ADT-3 2024-09" display.bin).
# Not the HY300 Pro (636 MHz, 2024-12 firmware). Silkscreen unknown on both: neither owner has opened the unit. Nobody
# here has the board; nothing of ours has run on it. Described from the owners' identify and h713-extract reads.
BOARD_ID=hy300-2023
VARIANTS="fw202306 fw202312"
STATUS=profile-only
VERIFIED_BY=
PROFILE=hy300_2023
IMAGE_NAME=h713-hy300-2023
# kernel patch 0350: the HY300 Pro's tree with the focus motor off (the case has a manual focus ring, no motor; no
# camera; a headphone jack). The display firmware is a revision nobody has run: its elog addresses and AFBD handoff
# words are unknown, the tree keeps the HY300 Pro's. Built with dtc, never booted.
KERNEL_DTB=sun50i-h713-hy300-2023
# U-Boot base hy300_2023_defconfig (fork h713-hy310 since 05.11.2026, mirror 0112): hy300_pro_defconfig with the HY350 family's DRAM block at
# 792 MHz (both owners' boot0, word for word), this tree and its identification string. Our HY300 Pro U-Boot at 636 MHz
# trained the DRAM of both for UMS (their reads, 04.11. and 11.11.2026). uboot.config beside this file keeps the same block for a probe build.
UBOOT_BOARD=hy300_2023
# Optional hardware: nothing measured. Both owners: no focus motor, no camera, a headphone jack, one button, a remote.
FEATURES=
# the name in the network (TODO 5.18)
HOSTNAME_BOARD=hy300
